# FE Design Principles — <%= projectName %>

<!-- arbiter-managed: frontend-governance (#1124) -->

**Framework:** <%= _fw %>
**Authority:** Binding project policy. Violations are defects, not style suggestions.

---

## P1: Semantic Tokens Only

Every color reference in UI templates MUST come from the semantic token layer.

- **NO** raw palette colors (`bg-amber-500`, `text-red-600`, `border-slate-200`)
- **NO** phantom tokens (undefined CSS vars produce zero CSS output → invisible elements)
- **NO** numbered shades outside the token system

**Why:** Semantic tokens are theme-aware. Raw palette classes break dark mode and require
per-component manual overrides. Using semantic tokens makes multi-theme correctness structural.

**Enforcement:** CI grep check for raw palette classes in UI source.

---

## P2: Page Header Consistency

All route-level views MUST use a shared `<PageHeader>` (or equivalent) component for
title/subtitle rendering. This enforces visual consistency across all pages.

**Exceptions (explicit, not default):**
- Dashboard — hero-card layout with custom visual hierarchy
- Auth / Error pages — centered full-page layouts
- Mobile execution views with full-bleed layouts

---

## P3: Explicit Component Imports (Runtime Safety)

Every component used in a template MUST have an explicit import in its script block.
Auto-import plugins are opt-in, not the default.

**Why:** Without explicit imports, a missing component renders as a raw HTML element
(e.g., `<appcard>`) with zero styling — invisible to users with no console error.
This is a runtime safety rule, not a style preference.

---

## P4: Container Heights Flow Down

The parent provides the height constraint. The child fills with `height: 100%`.

- **NEVER:** child forces a fixed height inside a smaller parent container
- **Pattern:** parent wraps with a fixed-height container, child chart/component uses `h-full`

**Why:** Prevents layout overflow and ensures chart/canvas components resize correctly.

---

## P5: Layout Fills Available Width

Page content containers MUST fill the layout shell's available width.
No `max-width` constraints on page content unless it is explicitly a reading layout.

**Why:** The layout shell controls the outer constraint. Per-page `max-width` overrides
create inconsistent widths across pages.

---

## P6: i18n Governance

All user-facing strings MUST use the i18n translation function (`t('key')`).
Keys MUST exist in all supported locale files. No raw UI literals.

**Enforcement:** CI grep check for unlocalized string literals in UI template files.

---

## P7: Visual Verification Protocol

Any layout or styling change requires:

1. **Unit tests** — component renders without crash
2. **Local visual verification** — rendered page inspected in browser
3. **Responsive check** — 375px mobile and 1280px desktop minimum
4. **Dark mode check** — verify no raw palette breakage

**Unit tests passing does NOT equal visual correctness.** Browser evidence is mandatory
for any visual claim.

---

## P8: Dark Mode by Design

Semantic tokens are theme-aware via CSS custom properties scoped to `[data-theme]`.
Raw palette colors break dark mode. Using semantic tokens makes dark-mode correctness
a structural guarantee, not a per-component concern.

**Corollary:** Every phantom token fix is simultaneously a dark-mode fix.

---

## P9: Accessibility by Default

All interactive elements MUST be keyboard-accessible and meet WCAG 2.1 AA contrast ratios.

- Form inputs MUST have associated labels (not just placeholder text).
- Icon-only buttons MUST have `aria-label` or equivalent.
- Focus indicators MUST be visible and not suppressed with `outline: none` without replacement.

**Enforcement:** Automated a11y checks in CI (e.g., axe-core Playwright integration).
